1- When it comes to Triggers, we could make a simple PR (Pull Request) or even a PE (Push Event) to be the main trigger to initiate the pipeline. 

2- The Jobs, I think, would be listed as follows (briefly):

- we will start from the testing phase
- installing the Python Packs/Libs
- making sure all Dependencies are there
- testing the API before initiation
- writing & applying the code/app
- running SonarCube to analyze the code and make sure it is free of syntax error (Code Logic and Code Quality)
- running an OWASP dependency check
- push to pre-prod
- make the Docker Image
- run Trivy & make Image Hardening

3- The Steps will be under the Jobs

4- The Artifact would be The Docker Image

5- The Env would be Staging (on GitHub)

6- The Fail Fast would be would of course be a failure in applying the code itself or having something wrong in the dependencies or logic. Even some in the security
